From 23ea50da6aa9814274471928f81b6f2fbb698e3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:11:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Ask for the provider before translating and offer
 re-translation

Tapping the Bilingual control used to start translating immediately
with the active profile. It now opens a single-choice picker of the
configured profiles first, so switching the engine for one video does
not require a detour through the settings.

- the picker marks entries that already cached this video and entries
  whose configuration is incomplete (tapping those explains instead
  of failing silently)
- picking a profile activates it and then starts the translation, so
  the player still resolves the bilingual track through the active
  configuration and finds the freshly cached file
- picking an already-cached profile asks whether to re-translate;
  confirming deletes the old cache files (vtt/done/meta) and starts
  over, replacing the previous translation
- BisubPrefs.configOf builds a Config from any profile regardless of
  which one is active; load() delegates to it
- BisubManager gains isTranslationCached, deleteTranslationCache and
  startTranslationWithProfile on top of a cfg-explicit
  resolveCacheTarget overload
